WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.939
Fail-secure authorization begins with a
non-authorized operation and requires

2
00:00:05.019 --> 00:00:08.429
positive, trusted evidence before any
protected side effect.

3
00:00:08.509 --> 00:00:13.270
Authentication establishes identity;
authorization evaluates whether that subject

4
00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:16.824
may perform this action on this resource
under current context.

5
00:00:16.904 --> 00:00:20.121
Missing identity, tenant, role, ownership,
object state,

6
00:00:20.201 --> 00:00:23.932
or action information cannot be replaced
with a permissive default.

7
00:00:24.012 --> 00:00:28.258
New actions and resources should remain
non-grant until an applicable policy

8
00:00:28.338 --> 00:00:29.754
explicitly handles them.

9
00:00:29.834 --> 00:00:31.442
Represent outcomes clearly.

10
00:00:31.522 --> 00:00:35.897
A Boolean is sufficient when its failure
contract is unambiguous and exceptions

11
00:00:35.977 --> 00:00:36.942
block execution.

12
00:00:37.022 --> 00:00:38.437
Use explicit allow, deny,

13
00:00:38.517 --> 00:00:42.892
and indeterminate variants when callers
need to preserve operational meaning.

14
00:00:42.972 --> 00:00:46.896
TypeScript exhaustiveness can identify
unhandled internal variants,

15
00:00:46.976 --> 00:00:50.708
while external policy responses still
require runtime validation.

16
00:00:50.788 --> 00:00:55.163
Denial and indeterminate both prevent the
action even when they map to different

17
00:00:55.243 --> 00:00:56.272
client responses.

18
00:00:56.352 --> 00:00:59.762
Bound dependency deadlines and retries,
validate responses,

19
00:00:59.842 --> 00:01:02.866
and ensure circuit breakers end in
non-grant behavior.

20
00:01:02.946 --> 00:01:06.291
Cache decisions only with keys, freshness,
policy-version,

21
00:01:06.371 --> 00:01:09.395
and revocation behavior appropriate to the
operation.

22
00:01:09.475 --> 00:01:12.820
Limited stale use may be a deliberate
availability tradeoff,

23
00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:16.374
but cache absence and unlimited stale
permits are not evidence.

24
00:01:16.454 --> 00:01:20.893
Preserve the required control flow through
middleware, services, workers, RPC,

25
00:01:20.973 --> 00:01:25.348
and administrative paths; await decisions
and make fall-through structurally

26
00:01:25.428 --> 00:01:26.136
impossible.

27
00:01:26.216 --> 00:01:30.012
Finally, test missing context, failures,
timeouts, invalid states,

28
00:01:30.092 --> 00:01:31.314
and cache boundaries.

29
00:01:31.394 --> 00:01:33.324
Verify that data, messages, files,

30
00:01:33.404 --> 00:01:37.650
and downstream calls remain untouched when
authorization is indeterminate.

31
00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:42.105
Observe infrastructure failure separately
from legitimate denial so teams can

32
00:01:42.185 --> 00:01:44.758
improve resilience without weakening
policy.

33
00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:48.248
When the application cannot establish that
access is allowed,

34
00:01:48.328 --> 00:01:50.580
uncertainty must not become permission.
